---
description: Payment confirmation must use verification/webhooks, amount checks, and idempotency
alwaysApply: true
---

# Payment security

- Never mark payment successful based solely on a frontend return URL.
- Confirm success via webhook and/or server-side payment verification (Bachs).
- Verify amount, currency (`NGN`), transaction reference, and booking before `Payment → SUCCESS` and `Booking → CONFIRMED`.
- Implement idempotency: the same webhook/reference must not double-confirm or double-charge.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — trust the return-URL query string
if (query.status === "success") confirmBooking(id);

// ✅ GOOD — verify with the provider, then persist once
const result = await payments.verify({ reference, bookingId });
if (alreadyProcessed(reference)) return;
assertAmountAndCurrency(result, payment);
```
